WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.124
A transfer moves money from an account on one shard to an account on another.

00:00:06.124 --> 00:00:10.248
But neither shard can see the other.

00:00:10.248 --> 00:00:14.371
If the first one commits and the second one crashes, the money simply vanishes.

00:00:14.371 --> 00:00:18.495
One machine being atomic is not enough.

00:00:18.495 --> 00:00:22.619
The shards need a protocol to commit together, or abort together, as one.

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:26.092
Here is the protocol, in two phases.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:29.565
In phase one, prepare, the coordinator asks every shard one question.

00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:33.037
Can you commit?

00:00:33.037 --> 00:00:36.510
Each shard writes its change to its own log and votes yes.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.983
The coordinator counts the votes.

00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:43.456
Does the transaction commit, or abort?

00:00:43.456 --> 00:00:46.928
They are all yes, so the decision is commit.

00:00:46.928 --> 00:00:50.401
A single no anywhere would force an abort instead, and the coordinator logs that decision before it tells anyone.

00:00:50.401 --> 00:00:53.874
Now phase two.

00:00:53.874 --> 00:00:57.347
The coordinator tells every shard to commit.

00:00:57.347 --> 00:01:00.819
Each shard applies the change and acknowledges it.

00:01:00.819 --> 00:01:04.292
The result is atomic across all three shards.

00:01:04.292 --> 00:01:07.765
All of them commit, or none of them do.

00:01:07.765 --> 00:01:13.152
There is a catch: the coordinator is a single point of failure.

00:01:13.152 --> 00:01:18.539
Crash it between prepare and decision, and every prepared shard is stuck, it cannot abort alone, cannot commit without the decision.

00:01:18.539 --> 00:01:23.926
Production fixes this with a consensus group.

00:01:23.926 --> 00:01:27.530
Two protocols, two jobs.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:31.134
Two-phase locking keeps one machine serializable; two-phase commit gets separate machines to agree on one outcome.

00:01:31.134 --> 00:01:34.737
A multi-shard transaction needs both.

00:01:34.737 --> 00:01:38.341
The weakness left is the single coordinator.

00:01:38.341 --> 00:01:41.945
Next: how a cluster elects a leader.
